Server created
  setup [OPTION]... [PORT] [DIR] : Setup the game server.
  start : Start the server.
  stop : Stop the server.
  restart : Stop the server and start it again.
  kill : Force-kill the server process immediately without a graceful shutdown.
  activate [OPTION]... : Set the server to restart on reboots and start now
        unless --delay is specified.
  deactivate [OPTION]... : Stop the server from restarting on reboots and stop
        now unless --delay is specified.
  status [OPTION]... : Check the status of the server. At the minimum will
        report if the server is running.
  send INPUT : Send a line of text directly to the server console (for admin
        commands, not player chat).
  message MESSAGE : Message the server. By default sends the message to all
        users.
  connect : Connect to the server's console session.
  logs [OPTION]... : Show the last lines of the server console log (default 50).
        Use -n to change the count.
  dump : Dump the servers data store.
  set [OPTION]... [KEY] [VALUE]... : Set a parameter in data store to a new
        value.
  backup : Backup the game server
  restore [BACKUP] : Restore the game server from a backup.
  wipe : Delete game-world data for supported server types.
  query : Query the game server to check whether it is responding.
  info [OPTION]... : Retrieve detailed server information: player count, map,
        version, etc.
  doctor : Print runtime diagnostics for this server, including the effective
        backend, Docker image/container details, and local runtime health
        checks.
The Sector-Alpha Game Server Management Script (AlphaGSM)

/media/cosmosquark/SSD/sector_alpha/github/AlphaGSM/alphagsm SERVER COMMAND [ARGS...]
/media/cosmosquark/SSD/sector_alpha/github/AlphaGSM/alphagsm COUNT SERVER... COMMAND [ARGS...]

SERVER is the server or servers to process. If a server is
specified as username/server then we use sudo to run as the
relevant user. This is always possible as root but is up to sudo
otherwise and may prompt for a password. The server can be the
special forms "*", which means apply to all the current user's
servers ("username/*" works too), or "*/*" which means run on a
command dependent definition of "all servers". This last form is
only available for a very limited set of commands.

If the second calling form is specified there must be EXACTLY
COUNT servers specified.



The available commands are:
  help [COMMAND] : Print a help message. Without a command print
                   this message or with a command print detailed help
                   for that command.
  create TYPE [setup ARGS] : Create a new server of the specified
                   type. If setup is specified then will call setup on
                   the new server immediately. ARGS is passed directly
                   on to setup so see there for the format and options
                   available.
  list : list the servers this is run on one per line. Useful for
                   checking what servers a wildcard matched or in
                   scripts to list the servers in a script processable
                   way.
  self-update [OPTION]... : Check for a newer AlphaGSM release and
                   apply it when supported.


